Wrapper code in this repository (app.py, fetch_weights.py, entrypoint.sh, Dockerfile) is Apache-2.0, see LICENSE.

The container image built from it contains:

- The `pocket-tts` Python package 4.0.1 (https://github.com/kyutai-labs/pocket-tts), MIT License, installed unchanged
  from PyPI. Its licence text ships in the image at /licenses/pocket-tts-LICENSE and in this repository as
  LICENSE-pocket-tts.
- The model weights from https://huggingface.co/kyutai/pocket-tts-without-voice-cloning (commit
  a7056f505a4a8ca72d8b5fb1440071d6f1a35739) and its tokenizer (commit 00eac05ed3d16bdc3f6b5d598874019c34a89214),
  by Kyutai, declared `license: cc-by-4.0` and ungated (read 2026-11-25). Licensed under Creative Commons
  Attribution 4.0 International; attribution: "Pocket TTS by Kyutai (Manu Orsini, Simon Rouard, Gabriel De Marmiesse,
  Vaclav Volhejn, Neil Zeghidour, Alexandre Defossez), CC BY 4.0, unmodified". The legal text ships in the image at
  /licenses/CC-BY-4.0-LICENSE and in this repository as LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0. The model card adds a prohibited-use
  paragraph, reproduced in README-marketplace.md.
- 19 preset voice embeddings from the same repository. Their source recordings (kyutai/tts-voices) are licensed:
  CC BY 4.0 for alba (Alba MacKenna), anna, vera, fantine, charles, paul, eponine, azelma, george, mary, jane,
  michael and eve (CSTR VCTK corpus, University of Edinburgh); CC0 for marius and javert (Unmute Voice Donation
  Project), and bill_boerst, peter_yearsley, stuart_bell and caro_davy (Voice-Zero, LibriVox). The voices `cosette`
  (Expresso) and `jean` (EARS) are CC BY-NC 4.0, non-commercial, and are deliberately NOT in this image.
- PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause, CPU wheel), NumPy (BSD-3-Clause), SoundFile (BSD-3-Clause) with libsndfile (LGPL-2.1), FastAPI
  (MIT), uvicorn (BSD-3-Clause) and the other Python dependencies pinned in requirements.txt, each under its own licence.

Voice cloning from an uploaded sample is not offered: the weights that contain the cloning encoder
(kyutai/pocket-tts) are gated, and this image carries the ungated ones. The model has no content filter and no
watermark. The operator is responsible for what the API is asked to say and for how the audio is used.
